{"id":"agreements-near-the-line","title":"Agreements raised to just under $10 million, then brought to the Board","question":"Before the Board voted on an agreement, how close to the $10 million line had the department already taken it?","finding":"Of 115 Board files whose executed agreements and modifications from before the Board item are in this download, 19 had a last ceiling between $9.5 million and $10 million; 10 of them are Airport agreements.","how":"Each executed agreement or modification attached to a Board file was read for its “not to exceed” amount and its date (from the file name, or the “made as of” line). Drafts are left out, and so is any document at or above the amount the Board item approves. The last ceiling before the Board item’s introduction date is compared with the $10 million line in Charter section 9.118(b). Every row was read by hand.","limits":"The files were downloaded because they reached the Board, so agreements that stayed under the line are missing and no fair expected share can be given. Amounts are read from scanned text and the date of an undated modification comes from its first page. A ceiling just under the line has ordinary causes: one-year terms renewed by a commission, budgets near $10 million, and the Charter itself, which leaves amounts under $10 million to departments and commissions.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"file","t":"Board file","type":"link"},{"k":"matter","t":"Matter","type":"text"},{"k":"steps","t":"Ceilings before the Board item","type":"text"},{"k":"lastBefore","t":"Last ceiling before the Board","type":"usd"},{"k":"underLine","t":"Under $10 million by","type":"usd"},{"k":"boardAmount","t":"Amount in the Board item","type":"usd"},{"k":"introduced","t":"Board item introduced","type":"date"},{"k":"retroactive","t":"Titled retroactive","type":"text"},{"k":"document","t":"Last executed document","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"file":{"t":"180422","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=3485595